<title>JAPAN: Yasunaga up on Mitsubishi Motors report.</title>
<headline>Yasunaga up on Mitsubishi Motors report.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-10-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of Yasunaga Corp rose in Friday morning trade to a new high for 1996, supported by a newspaper report about Mitsubishi Motors Corp car engines, traders said.</p>
<p>The share price of the car engine parts maker was up 80 yen at 1,860 yen at 0152 GMT. It briefly climbed to 1,920 yen. Volume was 337,000 shares.  </p>
<p>The report, in the business daily Nihon Keizai Shimbun, said AB Volvo had agreed with Mitsubishi that the Japanese carmaker would supply its gasoline direct injection fuel-efficient engine for cars Volvo makes in its joint venture with Mitsubishi.</p>
